id: pm-rl-9nlg
title: Recover external decision receipts across the HTTP-to-PM commit window
description: "A hard kill after a frozen decision endpoint executes but before the local PM metric note commits can lose the response and require reissuing the unresolved request. Local persisted decisions and logical samples replay once, but physical request and unknown token accounting require endpoint-side idempotency or receipt retrieval. Add a supported endpoint contract and kill-in-window acceptance before claiming exactly-once remote request spending."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T05:29:43.601Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-08T01:30:18.457Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: An endpoint supplies stable request-id idempotency or retrievable immutable receipts; a hard kill after remote completion before local receipt persistence resumes without a second physical inference; physical request and token accounting are reconciled from receipts
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T20:00:55.671Z",codex-sol,"Built-package reproduction confirmed with a real scratch tracker and a local receipt server: the server completed the first inference then dropped the HTTP response. Resume consumed eight logical samples and promoted twice, but performed nine physical inferences (expected eight). Test loads and executes the built package successfully; the behavioral assertion fails. Plan: opt-in immutable idempotency-v1 receipts, a durable per-loop namespace and content-bound per-query keys, receipt identity and physical/token accounting in metric events, plus hard-kill and network-window drills."
  "2026-10-07T20:13:46.178Z",codex-sol,"Implemented opt-in idempotency-v1: durable per-run UUID namespaces, programme/checkpoint/phase/index-bound request keys in body and Idempotency-Key header, validated immutable response identities and original physical/token/latency accounting in PM events. Eight real SIGKILL drills passed across both query phases at pre-dispatch, remote-completion, parsed-response and committed-note boundaries. Resume preserves eight physical inferences, eight logical decisions and 88 tokens. Legacy endpoints preserve their explicit non-idempotent boundary. Namespace/evidence corruption is refused before further HTTP requests. Full npm and Bun release gates and behavioral revert proof are pending."
  "2026-10-07T20:27:55.293Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof PASS: restored only the pre-fix bodies of requestSystemOneDecision (systemone.ts) and verifyDecisionPrefix (index.ts), retaining current signatures, exports, namespace persistence, crash hooks and all test files. npm run build succeeded. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"built receipt recovery|SIGKILL|received headers\" test/decision-recovery.test.ts executed three tests; each FAILED on physical inference accounting (9 actual versus 8 expected), including SIGKILL after remote completion. Fixed source was restored byte-for-byte and rebuilt. PM-linked recovery (6/6) and adapter (8/8) commands passed with no skips. Project policy disables automatic test-result recording, so this comment preserves the receipts. The initial full gate was stopped after new coverage cases were added; the final frozen-source gates will follow."
  "2026-10-07T20:28:48.043Z",codex-sol,"Restored-source validation PASS: npm run build:test and node --test test/decision-recovery.test.ts test/systemone.test.ts passed 14/14 tests, zero failures/skips after the behavioral revert proof. The implementation, tests and documentation are frozen for the required npm and Bun release gates; no PM SDK bug was observed in this recovery slice. Scratch trackers use explicit cwd and pmRoot to avoid inherited tracker context."
  "2026-10-07T20:41:53.896Z",codex-sol,"Review hardening and second revert proof PASS: stored receipt counts and latency must now match the canonical strings written by the package, decision ids must remain trimmed, and missing tags refuse with a typed drift error. Real tracker regressions add padded input/output token counts. The full focused suite passed 14/14 after this change. Restoring only the earlier verifySystemOneReceiptEvent body from implementation commit 670411b built successfully and made the real-tracker corruption test FAIL with Missing expected rejection: input-leading-zero. Fixed source was restored byte-for-byte and rebuilt. Source, tests and docs are now frozen for final npm/Bun release gates."
  "2026-10-07T21:08:36.229Z",codex-sol,"Final implementation fe69f39 PASS: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each exited zero with 439/439 tests, zero failures/skips, exact 100% statements/lines/branches/functions across all 24 authored source files including scripts, 227 documented declarations, no coverage exclusions or lowered thresholds, strict typecheck/build/lint, zero duplication, identity/publish-attestation checks, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog validation. Latest pm test pm-rl-9nlg --run --progress passed recovery 6/6 and adapter 8/8. Main revert: three executed behavioral failures at 9 versus 8 physical inferences; validator revert: real tracker padded-count rejection failed as expected. Both builds succeeded and fixed source was restored. Only tracking/documentation receipts follow; implementation and tests remain unchanged. No PM SDK bug observed. Immutable endpoint retention/idempotency is required; legacy endpoints retain their documented limitation. Item remains open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-07T21:10:34.867Z",codex-sol,"PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/65 is open against main on fix/decision-receipt-recovery. Implementation commits 670411b and fe69f39 contain the code and real regressions; e65bfce records both full gate receipts. Final source/tests remain byte-identical to gate-checked fe69f39. Claim is released, item remains open for orchestrator verification, and no merge/release/tag/publication occurred. README and durable validation include the endpoint contract, typed receipt surface, both revert proofs and gate evidence."
  "2026-10-08T00:50:45.009Z",codex-sol,"PR #65 review comment 4213484429 is valid: evidence completion permits a missing receipt namespace although inspection rejects it. Add the matching conflict guard before prefix verification and a real-tracker regression using the final decision commit callback to remove the namespace. Prove the regression fails with only the guard reverted, then run npm, Bun, and isolated-HOME release checks and regenerate the changelog."
  "2026-10-08T00:52:46.668Z",codex-sol,"Completion guard implemented before verifyDecisionPrefix; receipt-free endpoints retain the existing path. The real-tracker regression removes the namespace through the final held-out commit callback after all four HTTP decisions persist, asserts loop_generation_drift with EXIT_CODE.CONFLICT, unchanged event notes, no new candidate/evaluation items, and collection as the only completed phase. Initial revert verification exposed a fixture callback running again in generation two; bounding the fixture to one generation fixed the proof. Guard-only revert built successfully and FAILED with Missing expected rejection (1 executed, 1 failed); restoring source byte-for-byte and rebuilding made the regression PASS (1/1). Required full gates pending."
  "2026-10-08T00:54:07.875Z",codex-sol,"pm test pm-rl-9nlg --run --progress passed all three linked snapshot commands: node --test test/decision-recovery.test.ts (7/7), node --test test/systemone.test.ts (8/8), and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"evidence completion refuses\" test/decision-recovery.test.ts (1/1), each with zero failures/skips. Project policy disables automatic result recording; this comment retains the receipts. Code and test bytes are frozen for the three required release checks."
  "2026-10-08T01:30:17.653Z",codex-sol,"Final PR #65 review validation PASS: npm run release:check, bun run release:check, and env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check each exited zero with 440/440 tests, zero failures/skips, and exact 100% statements/lines/branches/functions across all 24 authored source files including operational scripts. All thresholds remain 100 with no exclusions. Each gate also passed strict typecheck/build/lint, zero duplication, 227 documented declarations, identity/publish-attestation checks, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry run and changelog validation. Source, tests and package configuration remained byte-identical across the three gates. Guard-only revert built and failed the completion regression with Missing expected rejection; restored guard passes. PM-linked commands passed 7/7, 8/8 and 1/1. The completion path now refuses a missing configured namespace before verifyDecisionPrefix and writes no subsequent evidence; receipt-free behavior is unchanged. No new scoped implementation risks found; remote exactly-once guarantees still require the documented endpoint receipt contract. Release the claim and leave the item in_progress for orchestrator verification; commit explicit code, tests, documentation and matching tracker/history paths as SteveBot and push the PR branch only."
